  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering Young Voices for Sustainable Urbanization</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The &#x201c;Empowering Young Voices for Sustainable Urbanization&#x201d; project seeks to enhance youth leadership and participation in urban development in Armenia, Colombia, and Otavalo, Ecuador. By integrating cultural preservation, environmental stewardship, and gender equity, the initiative empowers young people to address critical challenges such as environmental degradation, inadequate public spaces, and systemic gender inequality. The establishment of the Otavalango One Stop Youth Resource Centre serves as a regional hub for innovative solutions and capacity building, fostering community-driven approaches to sustainable urbanization. Through collaboration with local governments, international partners, and indigenous communities, the project aligns with the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) and the New Urban Agenda, creating a replicable model for inclusive, resilient, and culturally enriched urban development.</narrative>
  </description>
